# no private step of its own. E53_S10_T01 repointed it at the public idea-to-committed playbook and
# renamed it understand-then-commit, so it now ships publicly and is deliberately NOT listed here.
# The two real-catalog tests assert those now-private playbooks load against the real skills tree,
# so they follow their subjects out of the mirror per the E50_S07_T11 rule directly above. This is
# what turns the public suite's two failures green — because their subjects are private, NOT by
# weakening either assertion; both still run in full in the private repo.
# tests/load-playbooks-stepobject.bats: asserts the real brainstorm-to-mirror.json loads
tests/load-playbooks-stepobject.bats
# tests/load-playbooks-composition.bats: its real-catalog check used to assert the (then-private)
# understand-then-ship composition. Since E53_S10_T01 that check targets two PUBLIC playbooks
